# decision Setup embeds a thin released-version pointer skill

`git-a2a setup` installs exactly two embedded files: `thin/SKILL.md` and
`thin/references/README.md`. They direct an agent to the same binary's `usage --prompt` and
`explain` commands plus the canonical site, instead of copying the full documentation snapshot
into every consumer repository. `tools/sync-skill.py` keeps the thin frontmatter version equal to
`internal/version/VERSION` and rejects extra embedded files. The full `skills/git-a2a/` tree
remains byte-identical in the repository, npm, and site distributions. Setup remains offline and
never installs or upgrades the executable.
